> I recommend the +7 fooproof Excalibur. Archons prefer long swords over
> all other weapons and will not hang on to any other type of weapon.
> Pets do not know enchantment on weapons (as opposed to armor).

Pets pick up artifacts based on alignment.  Being lawful Archons will
not pick up artifacts that are chaotic or neutral.  I don't know if they
pick up unaligned artifacts.

> Getting your pet to unwield its current weapon is the hard part.

Not really.  If a pet picks up an artifact he will unwwield his current
weapon no matter what it is and wield the new artifact.  Pets do this
without considering weapon types.  Artifacts are the exception to the
list of weapons monsters will wield.

Knowing the combination of which artifacts a pet will pick up at all and
that they will swap to any new artifact is key to getting a pet to use
the artifact of your choice.  It can also happen that a pet switches
without a plan by you - Pick up off the floor.  You can give a pet a
weaker artifact to get him to swap away from a stronger artifact hoping
he will drop the stronger one for you to use.  You can give a pet a
stronger artifact as an upgrade knowing he'll switch to it as long as he
will pick it up.

None of that works if the pet is currently wielding a cursed weapon
because he can't put it down.  Since pets don't step on cursed items and
con't pick them up I don't know how to get a pet to wield a cursed
weapon.  It should be possible used some obscure skilled stunt.  It's
not a bad thing to wander through levels of undead with a pet who has
Werebane welded to his hand, but how to achieve that ...


